## Phase 3: Password Generation

If the user chooses to generate a new secure password:

```bash
# Ask for password complexity preferences
Via AskUserQuestion, ask:
> What type of password would you like to generate?
>
> - Simple (letters only, 12 chars)
> - Moderate (letters + numbers, 16 chars)
> - Strong (letters + numbers + symbols, 20 chars)
> - Extra Strong (letters + numbers + symbols, 24+ chars)
> - Custom (specify length and complexity)

# Based on choice, generate password using secure random
if [ "$CHOICE" = "Simple" ]; then
  PASSWORD=$(LC_ALL=C tr -dc 'a-zA-Z' < /dev/urandom | head -c 12)
elif [ "$CHOICE" = "Moderate" ]; then
  PASSWORD=$(LC_ALL=C tr -dc 'a-zA-Z0-9' < /dev/urandom | head -c 16)
elif [ "$CHOICE" = "Strong" ]; then
  PASSWORD=$(LC_ALL=C tr -dc 'a-zA-Z0-9!@#$%^&*()_+-=[]{};:,.<>?' < /dev/urandom | head -c 20)
elif [ "$CHOICE" = "Extra Strong" ]; then
  PASSWORD=$(LC_ALL=C tr -dc 'a-zA-Z0-9!@#$%^&*()_+-=[]{};:,.<>?' < /dev/urandom | head -c 24)
elif [ "$CHOICE" = "Custom" ]; then
  # Ask for custom specifications
  Via AskUserQuestion, ask:
  > Specify your custom password requirements:
  >
  > - Length (number of characters): [input]
  > - Include lowercase? (y/n): [input]
  > - Include uppercase? (y/n): [input]
  > - Include numbers? (y/n): [input]
  > - Include symbols? (y/n): [input]

  # Build character set based on responses
  CHARSET=""
  [ "$LOWER" = "y" ] && CHARSET="$CHARSETabcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz"
  [ "$UPPER" = "y" ] && CHARSET="$CHARSETABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ"
  [ "$NUMBERS" = "y" ] && CHARSET="$CHARSET0123456789"
  [ "$SYMBOLS" = "y" ] && CHARSET="$CHARSET!@#$%^&*()_+-=[]{};:,.<>?"

  # Generate password
  PASSWORD=$(LC_ALL=C tr -dc "$CHARSET" < /dev/urandom | head -c "$LENGTH")
fi

echo "Generated password: $PASSWORD"
```

```bash
# Ask if user wants to store this password
Via AskUserQuestion, ask:
> Would you like to store this password for future use?
>
> - Yes, store it (will prompt for website/username)
> - No, just use it once
```

If yes, proceed to Phase 4 to store the credential.

