## Phase 4: Adding/Storing Credentials

When storing a new credential (either from generation or manual input):

```bash
# Get credential details
Via AskUserQuestion, ask:
> Please provide the details for this credential:
>
> - Website or app name: [input]
> - Username/email: [input]
> - Password: [input]  # Will be hidden in actual implementation
> - Notes (optional): [input]
```

```bash
# Create credential object
CREDENTIAL=$(cat <<EOF
{
  "id": "$(date +%s%N)",
  "website": "$WEBSITE",
  "username": "$USERNAME",
  "password": "$PASSWORD",
  "notes": "$NOTES",
  "created_at": "$(date -Iseconds)",
  "updated_at": "$(date -Iseconds)"
}
EOF
)
```

```bash
# Add to storage (in real implementation, this would be encrypted)
# For now, we'll append to JSON array - in production this would use proper encryption
TEMP_FILE=$(mktemp)
jq ". += [$CREDENTIAL]" "$STORAGE_FILE" > "$TEMP_FILE" && mv "$TEMP_FILE" "$STORAGE_FILE"

echo "Credential for $WEBSITE stored successfully!"
```

