## Phase 6: Autofill Credentials

If user wants to autofill credentials on a website:

```bash
# Ask for target website
Via AskUserQuestion, ask:
> Which website would you like to autofill credentials on?
>
> - Enter website URL or name: [input]
```

```bash
# Search for matching credentials
# In real implementation, we'd decrypt storage and search
MATCHING_CREDS=$(jq -r --arg website "$WEBSITE" '.[] | select(.website | contains($website)) | "\(.id): \(.website) - \(.username)"' "$STORAGE_FILE")

if [ -z "$MATCHING_CREDS" ]; then
  echo "No credentials found for website: $WEBSITE"
else
  echo "Found matching credentials:"
  echo "$MATCHING_CREDS"

  # Ask which credential to use
  Via AskUserQuestion, ask:
  > Which credential would you like to use for autofill? (Enter ID or number from list)
  >
  > Options:
  > $MATCHING_CREDS
  > - Cancel
```

If user selects a credential:
```bash
# Get the full credential details
CREDENTIAL=$(jq -r --arg id "$SELECTED_ID" '.[] | select(.id == ($id|tonumber))' "$STORAGE_FILE")

# Extract username and password
USERNAME=$(echo "$CREDENTIAL" | jq -r '.username')
PASSWORD=$(echo "$CREDENTIAL" | jq -r '.password')

# Use browse skill to autofill
echo "Navigating to website for autofill..."
$B goto "$WEBSITE_URL"

# Wait for page to load, then attempt to fill form
$B snapshot -i  # Show interactive elements for user to confirm

Via AskUserQuestion, ask:
> Do you see the username and password fields on this page?
>
> - Yes, proceed with autofill
> - No, I'll fill manually
> - Cancel

If yes:
  $B fill @username_field "$USERNAME"
  $B fill @password_field "$PASSWORD"
  $B click @submit_button  # Or however the form is submitted

  echo "Credentials have been autofilled!"
  echo "Please review and submit the form manually if needed."
```

